# Strong, long-lived scroll wind

Status: DONE
Milestone: M63 Broad scroll-driven cloth gusts
Dependencies: 43_STRONGER_LINGERING_CLOTH.todo

## Purpose

Make the awning react much more strongly to scrolling and continue billowing
well after scrolling stops, like a gust of wind.

## Tasks

- [x] Preserve previous model/reviewers and measure the old response.
- [x] Add18seconds of travelling pressure, stronger immediate kick and smooth decay.
- [x] Preserve exact pointer-only trajectories, fixed rails/ends and displacement bounds.
- [x] Check repeated/reversed input, bounded extremes, reset and eventual exact idle.
- [x] Complete isolated175file baseline proof without touching the533file import candidate.
- [x] Run actual-GPU wind, existing cloth safety and full site/entry reviews locally.
- [x] Publish only the reviewed cloth/cache HTML/ABOUT changes.
- [x] Record live behavior/bytes and preserve the unpublished archive candidate.

## Acceptance criteria

- Strong broad response, continuing meaningful waves at10-14seconds after scroll.
- Wind stops completely at finite idle; no perpetual renderer loop.
- Reduced motion, print, forced colours, blur, hidden/offscreen states and dialogs stop motion.
- Fixed supports, artwork,2Mpixel budget and20pxcanvas gutter remain unchanged.
- No implicit archive publication or unnecessary static artwork regeneration.

